  <div id="sutta">
  
          <h4 id="thig13.2" class="h1">Thig 13:2  Rohiṇī</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p class="vspk">Rohiṇī’s father:</p>
            <p>You go to sleep saying,</p>
            <p class="v2">“Contemplatives.”</p>
            <p>You wake up,</p>
            <p class="v2">“Contemplatives.”</p>
            <p>You praise only</p>
            <p class="v2">contemplatives.</p>
            <p>No doubt you will be</p>
            <p class="v2">a contemplative.</p>
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Abundant food &amp; drink</p>
              <p>you give to contemplatives.</p>
              <p>Now, Rohiṇī, I ask you:</p>
              <p class="v2">Why do you hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear?</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>They don’t like to work,</p>
              <p>they’re lazy,</p>
              <p>living off what’s given by others,</p>
              <p>full of hankerings,</p>
              <p>wanting delicious things:</p>
              <p class="v2">Why do you hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear?</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="vspk">Rohiṇī:</p>
              <p>For a long time, father,</p>
              <p>you’ve quizzed me</p>
              <p>about contemplatives.</p>
              <p>I’ll praise to you</p>
              <p>their</p>
              <p class="v2">discernment,</p>
              <p class="v2">virtue,</p>
              <p class="v2">endeavor.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>They do like to work,</p>
              <p>they’re not lazy.</p>
              <p>They do the best work:</p>
              <p>They abandon</p>
              <p>passion &amp; anger.</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>They rid themselves</p>
              <p>of the three evil roots,<span class="fn"><a href="#thig13.2note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
              <p>doing pure actions.</p>
              <p>All their evil’s</p>
              <p>abandoned.</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Clean their bodily action,</p>
              <p>so is     their verbal action.</p>
              <p>Clean     their mental action:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Spotless, like mother of pearl,</p>
              <p>pure within &amp; without,</p>
              <p>perfect in clear qualities:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Learned,     maintaining the Dhamma,</p>
              <p>noble,     living the Dhamma,</p>
              <p>they teach the goal</p>
              <p>&amp; the Dhamma:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Learned,     maintaining the Dhamma,</p>
              <p>noble,     living the Dhamma,</p>
              <p>with unified minds</p>
              <p>&amp; mindful:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Traveling far, mindful,</p>
              <p>giving counsel unruffled,</p>
              <p>they discern the end</p>
              <p>of suffering:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>When they leave any village</p>
              <p>they don’t turn to look back</p>
              <p>at anything.</p>
              <p>How free from concern</p>
              <p>they go!</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>They don’t store in a granary,</p>
              <p>pot,</p>
              <p>or basket.</p>
              <p>They hunt [only]</p>
              <p>for what’s already cooked:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>They take neither silver,</p>
              <p>nor gold,</p>
              <p>nor money.</p>
              <p>They live off whatever is present:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>Having gone forth</p>
              <p>from different families</p>
              <p>&amp; from different countries,</p>
              <p>still they hold</p>
              <p>one another dear:</p>
              <p class="v2">That’s why I hold</p>
              <p class="v2">contemplatives dear.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="vspk">Rohiṇī’s father:</p>
              <p>Rohiṇī, truly for our benefit</p>
              <p>were you born in our family.</p>
              <p>You have conviction</p>
              <p>in the Buddha &amp; Dhamma,</p>
              <p>and strong respect</p>
              <p>for the Saṅgha.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p>You truly discern</p>
              <p>this field of merit</p>
              <p>unexcelled.</p>
              <p>These contemplatives will receive</p>
              <p><em>our</em> offering, too,</p>
              <p>for here we’ll set up</p>
              <p>our abundant sacrifice.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="vspk">Rohiṇī:</p>
              <p>If you’re afraid of pain,</p>
              <p>if you dislike pain,</p>
              <p>go to the Buddha for refuge,</p>
              <p>go to the Dhamma &amp; Saṅgha.</p>
              <p>Take on the precepts:</p>
              <p class="v2">That will lead</p>
              <p class="v2">to your benefit.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="vspk">Rohiṇī’s father:</p>
              <p>I go to the Buddha for refuge;</p>
              <p>I go to the Dhamma &amp; Saṅgha.</p>
              <p>I take on the precepts:</p>
              <p class="v2">That will lead</p>
              <p class="v2">to my benefit.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
            <div class="verse-add">
              <p class="verse_stars">* * *</p>
              <p>Before, I was a kinsman to Brahmā;</p>
              <p>now, truly a brahman.</p>
              <p>I’m a three-knowledge man &amp; safe,</p>
              <p>consummate in knowledge,</p>
              <p class="v2">washed clean.</p>
            </div><!--end verse-add-->
          </div><!--end verse-->
          <div class="note">
            <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
            <p id="thig13.2note01">1. The three unskillful roots are greed, aversion, and delusion. See <a href="../../DN/DN02.html">DN 2</a>, <a href="../../MN/MN9.html">MN 9</a>, and <a href="../../AN/AN3_66.html">AN 3:66</a>.</p>
          </div><!--end notes-->
          <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../../SN/SN7_17.html">SN 7:17</a>; <a href="../StNp/StNp1_4.html">Sn 1:4</a></p><!--end seealso-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
